data: {"seq":1472,"emitted_at":"2026-09-14T02:54:15.539562201Z","session_id":"0b1k44-audio","event":{"type":"ask_user_question","prompt_id":"01a09dd5-c146-7b51-92a2-e11f08a3585f","interrogative_id":"01a09dd6-31f3-7530-b368-5ca3f5bd42d9","payload":{"questions":[{"id":"untracked-script","context":"# Where this question comes from\n\nYou asked me to exercise my structured question tool, so I picked the most decision-relevant thing I can actually see in this session.\n\n## Current repository state\n\n- **Branch:** `feat/notify-cleanup` (default branch: `main`)\n- **Working tree:** dirty — one untracked file: `scripts/capture-probe-events.sh`\n\nThat untracked shell script is the only thing standing between this branch and a clean tree. As the product-design facet I don't write files myself, but this decision shapes how I'd frame any planning or handoff for this session: whether the script is part of the notify-cleanup deliverable, a temporary probe that should stay local, or clutter to remove.\n\n## Options and tradeoffs\n\n- **Commit it here** — the probe script becomes part of the branch's history and any handoff plan can reference it as an in-scope artifact.\n- **Keep it untracked** — treat it as a local debug/probe tool; plans would exclude it from scope, and it stays invisible to git until you decide otherwise.\n- **Delete it** — clean up, though I'd suggest a quick read of it first so we know if it captures anything hard to recreate.\n\nIf it's something else entirely (e.g. it belongs on a different branch or should move elsewhere), use the free-text answer.","question":"What should happen with the untracked file `scripts/capture-probe-events.sh` on `feat/notify-cleanup`?","mode":"single_select","allow_free_text":true,"options":[{"id":"commit-here","label":"Commit it on this branch (Recommended)","description":"Add scripts/capture-probe-events.sh to feat/notify-cleanup as part of this branch's work.","justification":"Probe/capture scripts usually support the branch's validation story; tracking it keeps the deliverable self-contained and handoff-safe."},{"id":"keep-local","label":"Keep it untracked for now","description":"Treat it as a local-only tool; it stays untracked and out of scope for any plan."},{"id":"delete","label":"Delete it","description":"Remove the file to get a clean working tree (irreversible unless it's recoverable elsewhere)."}]}]}}}
data: {"seq":5704,"emitted_at":"2026-09-14T02:58:52.424591895Z","session_id":"0b1k44-audio","event":{"type":"ask_user_question","prompt_id":"01a09dd9-3c60-7db0-bd80-61f576f56409","interrogative_id":"01a09dda-6b88-7360-8697-979523062e33","payload":{"questions":[{"id":"execute-scope","context":"# Why I'm asking instead of switching now\n\nFacet switches here go through `handoff_plan`, and that tool carries the **active plan document** — but no plan has been written this session. The only recorded work so far is the joke goal (delivered: hello 👋, ready to close) and your \"keep the probe script untracked\" decision (no action). A handoff with an empty plan would be process fiction, and my facet contract requires every plan to record git-target answers before it's written.\n\nSo before I can propose the switch concretely, I need to know what the `execute` facet would actually take up.\n\n## One routing note\n\nMy lifecycle normally routes plan approval to the `project-manager` facet (design → PM → implementation). You've asked for `execute` directly — direct requests take precedence, so I can target `execute`; just flagging that I'm deviating from the default routing on your say-so.\n\n## What happens after you answer\n\n1. If there's real work: I fire the git-target gate (branch / worktree / disposition), frame the design, write the plan, then submit `handoff_plan` for your review.\n2. If there's nothing: I write a minimal closeout plan (goal delivered, script stays untracked, tree otherwise untouched) and hand that off so the switch is still reviewable.","question":"What should the `execute` facet take up when control is handed over?","mode":"single_select","allow_free_text":true,"options":[{"id":"nothing","label":"Nothing to implement — closeout only","description":"The greeting goal is delivered and the script decision needs no action — execute receives control with an empty backlog via a minimal closeout plan."},{"id":"notify-cleanup","label":"Continue the notify-cleanup work","description":"Frame and hand off the actual notify-cleanup work this branch exists for (I'll investigate scope, then run the git-target gate)."}]}]}}}
data: {"seq":10452,"emitted_at":"2026-09-14T03:04:53.051669344Z","session_id":"0b1k44-audio","event":{"type":"interrogative","prompt_id":"01a09dde-f338-76f0-8520-dffd849a62e5","interrogative_id":"01a09ddf-ec3b-7822-b95f-85ace3e81239","question":"Approve plan?","interrogative_type":"plan_handoff","plan_handoff":{"plan_path":"/home/dev/.local/share/polytoken/sessions/0b1k44-audio/plan-001.md","display_path":"/home/dev/.local/share/polytoken/sessions/0b1k44-audio/plan-001.md","plan_text":"# Plan: Session closeout & greeting handoff\n\n## Git target (mandatory section)\n\nGate **skipped with rationale**: scope is unambiguously non-mutating (greetings only; zero tracked-file changes), which qualifies as the pure-discussion skip path. Recorded dispositions from this session's operator answers apply verbatim:\n\n- **Target branch:** none — no branch operations. Current branch `feat/notify-cleanup` is left exactly as-is.\n- **Worktree:** none — no disposable worktree is created or needed.\n- **Disposition:** none — no merge, no branch deletion, no tracked-file changes.\n\nAny future request that could plausibly touch tracked files returns to design and fires the full git-target gate.\n\n## Desired outcome\n\nThe `execute` facet takes control of the session with one ongoing mandate: **greet the operator** — say \"hello\" to them liberally and on cue. The operator is testing notification banners; the greeting flow itself is the deliverable.\n\n## Boundaries (non-goals)\n\n- No tracked-file changes of any kind — no commits, no edits, no new tracked files.\n- `scripts/capture-probe-events.sh` stays **untracked** (operator decision, recorded this session).\n- No branch creation, no merges, no worktrees.\n- No installs, no process control, no repository mutation.\n- The actual `feat/notify-cleanup` feature work is explicitly **out of scope** and remains unscoped for a future design pass.\n\n## Tasks\n\n1. **Receive the greeting mandate.** Execute confirms the scope: emit \"hello\" to the operator, as often as they enjoy.\n2. **Emit greetings on cue and unprompted** wherever a natural turn boundary allows. Each hello is complete in itself — no follow-up work, no files, no branches.\n3. **Keep the tree clean.** Do nothing that alters `git status` beyond the pre-existing untracked script.\n\n## Validation & acceptance criteria\n\n- Operator receives visible \"hello\" messages during the execute facet's tenure. (Primary criterion — this is the whole plan.)\n- `git status` at handoff close matches the session-start snapshot: only `?? scripts/capture-probe-events.sh`, still untracked.\n- Zero new commits on `feat/notify-cleanup`.\n\n## Prior dispositions carried forward\n\n- Untracked probe script: **keep untracked** (operator, this session).\n- Joke goal \"Greet the operator\": first hello delivered in design facet; todo #1 closed. This plan extends the joke into a standing mandate with the operator's full knowledge and consent.\n\n## Routing note\n\nHandoff is targeted to **`execute`** per the operator's explicit request, deliberately deviating from the default design → `project-manager` approval routing. Operator reviewed this plan document via the handoff banner they asked for.\n\n## Consultation\n\nNo specialist consultation: zero-risk, non-material plan (no code, no data, no lifecycle changes). Plan-reviewer round ran to completion (the operator's cancellation raced its exit; job `plan-reviewer:plan-review-closeout`): shape adequate, no material risk, zero critical/high findings, one low finding (this section's stale waiver claim) — resolved by this line. The operator directed immediate handoff regardless.\n","target_facet":"execute","title":"Approve plan?","action_labels":{"implement_new_context":"Implement plan with a new context","implement_current_context":"Implement plan within current context","cancel":"Refuse (Tab to add feedback)","refuse":"Feedback (Shift+Enter/Alt+Enter newline, Ctrl+Up to exit):"}}}}
